{"availability":"available","full":"goyashek/signature-forgery-verification","name":"signature-forgery-verification","description":"Leak-audited, writer-independent signature forgery verification using Siamese metric learning and EfficientNet-B0.","category":"Education","language":"Jupyter Notebook","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-06-27T18:11:23Z","updated":"2026-07-31T10:21:42Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/goyashek/signature-forgery-verification","topics":["computer-vision","efficientnet","gradio","siamese-network","signature-verification","tensorflow"],"demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/goyashek/signature-forgery-verification","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T22:33:57.452Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T22:33:57.452Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T22:33:57.452Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T22:33:57.452Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["🚀 Try the live demo · 📓 View notebook · ▶ Run in Colab","This project verifies whether a questioned offline signature matches an enrolled writer. Instead of training one classifier per person, it learns a distance metric over signatures, allowing the model to assess writers absent from training using a small reference set.","I built it as a learning progression: start with a naive baseline, investigate why it fails, and work toward the final metric-learning model. The final model is demonstrated in notebooks/04finaldemo.ipynb and served through a Gradio app on Hugging Face Spaces."],"features":["Task: Verify whether a questioned offline signature matches an enrolled writer.","Best model: EfficientNet-B0 + online batch-hard metric learning","Held-out benchmark: ROC-AUC 0.986 on unseen writers","External benchmark: ROC-AUC 0.877 on NFI","Main finding: A suspicious 0.999 baseline exposed two dataset leaks, so I rebuilt the pairing and evaluation protocol."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/goyas